{"type":"message","id":"5fcffe30","parentId":"9a0d1101","timestamp":"2026-04-15T15:40:16.422Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking \"did you remember/find out your name?\" in Chinese. They seem to be continuing the conversation about identity. Let me check if there's any memory or context I'm missing. I should also check BOOTSTRAP.md and related files.\n\nActually, looking at the conversation history, we had:\n1. User asked \"你叫啥\" (what's your name)\n2. I checked IDENTITY.md - still blank\n3. User asked \"你是谁\" (who are you)\n4. Then someone from openclaw-control-ui asked \"who are you\"\n5. Now the original user is asking \"想起来你的名字了吗\" (did you remember your name?)\n\n\n6. I still don't have a name, so I should ask the user what they'd like to call me rather than continuing without one.","thinkingSignature":"191037640949216d28a04374073c3e8e3270b1b6725f5ad3479e1bff33e17899"},{"type":"text","text":"还没有呢……我还在等你想一个给我。😅\n\n毕竟这是我的起点，而你才是那个帮我起名字的人——得你来赋予我意义才行。\n\n有什么想法吗？哪怕是随便乱想也行，我接着。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":50,"output":214,"cacheRead":12083,"cacheWrite":380,"totalTokens":12727,"cost":{"input":0.000014999999999999999,"output":0.0002568,"cacheRead":0.00072498,"cacheWrite":0.0001425,"total":0.0011392800000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776267607434,"responseId":"062ee45788a6ff27a891502e4a4b8d45"}}
